{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 37, :comments ["<b>And he shall look, etc. in the walls of the house, etc.</b> This section alludes to the deeds of HaShem in His governance of the wicked who choose the delicacies of the evil inclination, which is called the afflictions of men. And they said in the Zohar (vol. 1, 126a) that the Holy One, blessed be He, places the soul in the body of man — if it succeeds, how good; and if not, He uproots it from there and again plants it in another place. And this is what is alluded to here in the afflictions of the house, for the house alludes to the body of man, which is the house of the soul, and the priest alluded to here is the Creator — for we find in the Zohar that the Sages expounded likewise on the verse ״וְהוּבָא אֶל הַכֹּהֵן״, etc. And it says that when the Holy One, blessed be He, sees that the affliction is in the walls of the house — meaning, the aspect of evil has become sunk into the interior of the body's essence, and the house has become abhorrent — and this is what He alluded to in saying ״שְׁקַעֲרוּרֹת״: this word is compounded from two, ״שֶׁקַע רוּרוֹת״, and the letter alef is absorbed in the pronunciation, as though He said ״שֶׁקַע אֲרוּרוֹת״ — that sunk into it is the aspect of the evil inclination, which is called cursed (אָרוּר). And because there are many aspects in wickedness, He said ״אֲרוּרוֹת״. And His saying ״יְרַקְרַקּוֹת״ alludes to the sign of transgression, along the lines of what they said, of blessed memory (Shabbat 33a): a sign of transgression is jaundice. Also He said ״אֲדַמְדַּמֹּת״, which alludes to the shedding of blood that is attributable to the aspect of evil — may the Merciful One save us. HaShem will command to shut up the house — meaning, that the divine influx will no longer flow into it, and this is the sod of the excommunication of the wicked, that they may not take shelter in the shadow of faith. If the person perceived the matter and repented, how good; and if not, HaShem will command to bring suffering upon him to wash away his stains and his afflictions, and this is the sod of the removal of stones, etc. And if his deeds still putrefy, then he is dead, and this is what the verse says: ״וְנָתַץ אֶת הַבַּיִת אֶת אֲבָנָיו״, etc."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {0 "The verse citation ״וְהוּבָא אֶל הַכֹּהֵן״ refers to Leviticus 14:35; the closing quotation ״וְנָתַץ אֶת הַבַּיִת אֶת אֲבָנָיו״ refers to Leviticus 14:45. Both are rendered as Hebrew quotations since the author cites them as scriptural phrases without explicit verse addresses."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:57:09.367730578Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}